1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,867
Why worship the Sun on Chhath?

2
00:00:01,867 --> 00:00:04,667
The answer is hidden in Yudhishthir's vessel.

3
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:07,280
In the last story, we met Chhathi Maiya...

4
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:09,408
Meaning Goddess Shashti. Today,

5
00:00:09,408 --> 00:00:11,295
let's talk about the Sun God,

6
00:00:11,295 --> 00:00:13,052
the second deity of Chhath.

7
00:00:13,052 --> 00:00:15,200
Having lost everything at dice...

8
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:17,399
the Pandavas set off for exile...

9
00:00:17,399 --> 00:00:20,219
and many Brahmins followed right behind them.

10
00:00:20,219 --> 00:00:22,100
Yudhishthir sank into worry...

11
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:23,850
they have come trusting me,

12
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,154
I cannot abandon them,

13
00:00:25,154 --> 00:00:27,050
and I have nothing to feed them.

14
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:30,981
Then Priest Dhaumya showed the way,

15
00:00:30,981 --> 00:00:33,230
found in the Mahabharata's Vana Parva.

16
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:35,899
The Sun raises water with its rays...

17
00:00:35,899 --> 00:00:38,645
which returns as rain... and crops grow.

18
00:00:38,645 --> 00:00:41,390
Therefore, the Sun is the father of all.

19
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:44,220
Standing in the stream, facing the Sun,

20
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:46,708
Chanting his 108 names,

21
00:00:46,708 --> 00:00:48,684
the blazing Sun God appeared.

22
00:00:48,684 --> 00:00:50,320
Take this copper vessel.

23
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:51,820
Until Draupadi eats...

24
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:53,978
The food here will never run out.

25
00:00:53,978 --> 00:00:56,682
This vessel is known today as Akshaya Patra.

26
00:00:56,682 --> 00:00:59,140
Brahmins ate first... and Draupadi last.

27
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:00,507
As soon as she ate,

28
00:01:00,507 --> 00:01:02,426
that day's food was complete.

29
00:01:02,426 --> 00:01:04,610
So why worship the Sun on Chhath?

30
00:01:04,610 --> 00:01:06,860
Because the Sun provides the food.

31
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:09,026
And the Sun is the only deity...

32
00:01:09,026 --> 00:01:11,711
whom we see with our own eyes every day...

33
00:01:11,711 --> 00:01:14,140
therefore he is called a direct deity.

34
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:17,138
The name Chhath is not in the Mahabharata,

35
00:01:17,138 --> 00:01:19,810
yet the Vana Parva clearly states this.

36
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:23,600
Today, during Chhath, the worshippers...

37
00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:24,780
standing in water,

38
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:27,097
offer new grains and fruits to the Sun.

39
00:01:27,097 --> 00:01:29,950
The first offering goes to the provider of food.

40
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:32,830
In every home, there is someone...

41
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:34,305
who feeds everyone...

42
00:01:34,305 --> 00:01:35,781
and eats last of all.

43
00:01:35,781 --> 00:01:37,960
And perhaps they even wonder...

44
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:41,190
who will take care of me? Pay attention...

45
00:01:42,570 --> 00:01:44,886
The vessel kept filling until Draupadi ate.

46
00:01:44,886 --> 00:01:46,072
The one eating last...

47
00:01:46,072 --> 00:01:47,580
is the home's Akshaya Patra.

48
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:48,759
Try this today...

49
00:01:48,759 --> 00:01:51,279
whoever eats last in the house today...

50
00:01:51,279 --> 00:01:52,830
feed them first today...

51
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:58,075
or simply sit and eat with them.

52
00:01:58,075 --> 00:01:58,802
Next story?

53
00:01:58,802 --> 00:02:01,181
The world worships the rising sun...

54
00:02:01,181 --> 00:02:03,560
Chhath worships the setting one too.

55
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:06,024
Why? And send this story to the one...

56
00:02:06,024 --> 00:02:07,690
who eats last in the house.

